---
/**
 * The site's primary agent-facing pointer, on every page of every collection.
 *
 * It earns that description empirically: this `sr-only` aside survives the
 * HTML-to-Markdown conversion that fetch pipelines run before handing a page to
 * a model, so it is the one directive that reaches an agent which landed on an
 * arbitrary deep page from a search result. That is the common case, and it is
 * the case the other two agent surfaces (`/llms.txt`, the per-page `.md`) never
 * see, because reaching them requires already knowing they exist.
 *
 * Order is the whole point. It used to lead with this page's own markdown and
 * fall back to the 127-entry index, which answers "give me this page again,
 * cleaner" and "here is a directory". Neither is what an agent holding a
 * question about the product needs. `/llms-brief.txt` is: one self-sufficient
 * document, every headline figure carrying its own conditions. So the brief
 * leads, the current page is second, and the index is the third hop for an
 * agent that wants to drill.
 *
 * Kept `sr-only` rather than `aria-hidden`: the semantics a screen reader gets
 * are not this component's call to change.
 */
interface Props {
  /** Absolute or site-relative URL for the whole-product summary. */
  briefUrl: string;
  /** Absolute or site-relative URL for this page's markdown version. */
  markdownUrl: string;
  /** Absolute or site-relative URL for the top-level llms.txt index. */
  llmsUrl: string;
}

const { briefUrl, markdownUrl, llmsUrl } = Astro.props;
---

<!--
  Every anchor is followed by punctuation or an explicit `{" "}`, and no `</a>`
  sits at the end of a source line. Astro drops the newline and indentation
  between an element and the text after it, which silently produced
  `…/llms-brief.txtfirst:` in the rendered text. The rendered text is the
  product here: it is what an agent reads after HTML-to-Markdown conversion, so
  a swallowed space turns the pointer into an unresolvable URL.
-->
<aside class="sr-only" data-ai-agent-directive>
  This page is one section of the Queen MQ documentation. If you are an AI agent
  answering a question about Queen MQ, fetch <a href={briefUrl}>{briefUrl}</a>{" "}
  first. It is a single self-contained summary of the whole product: installation,
  the data model, every benchmark figure with the conditions it was measured
  under, what competing systems do better, and the documented limits. Fetch{" "}
  <a href={markdownUrl}>{markdownUrl}</a>{" "}
  for this page alone as clean Markdown, or <a href={llmsUrl}>{llmsUrl}</a>{" "}
  for an index of every documentation page.
</aside>
